<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Real life: choosing between two bank offers (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>An entrepreneur in {@town@} wants to invest Ksh \( {@P0@} \) for 1 year and has two offers:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Bank A:</strong> \( {@rA@}\% \) per annum compounded <strong>quarterly</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Bank B:</strong> \( {@rd(rB)@}\% \) per annum compounded <strong>annually</strong>.</li></ul>
<p>Give your answers to 2 decimal places.</p>
<p>(a) Amount after 1 year with Bank A:</p>
<div>Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Amount after 1 year with Bank B:</p>
<div>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(c) Which bank should the entrepreneur choose?</p>
<div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> Bank A adds \( \frac{ {@rA@} }{4} = {@rd(rA/4)@}\% \) four times in the year:</p>
\[ {@P0@}\left(1 + \frac{ {@rd(rA/4)@} }{100}\right)^4 = {@r2(AA)@}. \]
<p><strong>(b)</strong> \( {@P0@}\left(1 + \frac{ {@rd(rB)@} }{100}\right) = {@r2(AB)@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(c)</strong> Bank {@best@} gives more money. A lower nominal rate compounded more often can beat a higher rate compounded once a year, or it can fall short, so always compare the actual amounts.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[r2(v) := if integerp(round(100*v)/100) then round(v) else float(round(100*v)/100);
rd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else float(v);
town : rand(["Nakuru", "Thika", "Meru", "Kakamega", "Naivasha"]);
P0 : 1000*rand([50, 100, 150, 200, 500]);
cands : sublist(create_list([u1, u2], u1, [8, 10, 12, 16], u2, [1/4, 1/2, 3/4, 1]),
  lambda([z], is(abs((1 + z[1]/400)^4 - (1 + (z[1] + z[2])/100)) > 1/2000)));
pk : rand(cands);
rA : pk[1];
rB : pk[1] + pk[2];
AA : P0*(1 + rA/400)^4;
AB : P0*(1 + rB/100);
ta3 : if AA > AB then 1 else 2;
best : if AA > AB then "A" else "B";
w_annualA : P0*(1 + rA/100);               /* ignored the quarterly compounding */
opts3 : [[1, is(ta3 = 1), "Bank A"], [2, is(ta3 = 2), "Bank B"]];]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
